<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering" style="font-size:80%;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 5: </span>Distribution over the implicit and multi-step properties (§<a href="#S2" title="2 Strategy Questions ‣ Did Aristotle Use a Laptop? A Question Answering Benchmark with Implicit Reasoning Strategies" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>) in a sample of 100 <span id="S4.T5.14" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">StrategyQA</span> questions, annotated by two experts (we average the expert decisions).
Most questions are <em id="S4.T5.15" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">multi-step</em> and <em id="S4.T5.16" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">implicit</em>. Annotator agreement is substantial for both the implicit (<math id="S4.T5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa=0.73" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.73</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa=0.73</annotation></semantics></math>) and multi-step (<math id="S4.T5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa=0.65" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.65</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa=0.65</annotation></semantics></math>) properties.
</figcaption>
